{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And it was on the way, at the lodging.</b> This verse ought to be joined to 'and Moses took his wife and his sons' — just as 'he shall surely pay' (שלם ישלם) is joined to 'five oxen he shall pay in place of the ox.' But because the matter was communicated to him at the time of the journey, he interrupted in between." "<b>And He encountered him.</b> In the language of 'I will encounter them like a bereaved bear' (אפגשם כדוב שכול) (Hosea 13:8)." "<b>And He sought to put him to death.</b> Rabban Gamliel says: the infant, as it says 'for a bridegroom of blood you are to me.' Go and see: who is called 'bridegroom' — either Moses or the infant? You must say: the infant. Another interpretation: <b>and He sought to put him to death</b> — Moses, for he should have circumcised his son and left him with his mother and gone alone in haste on his mission from the Place (i.e., HaShem). But he went slowly on account of his wife and sons whom he took with him." "<b>And He sought to put him to death.</b> Rashi explains: and why was he punished? Because he occupied himself with the lodging first. And if you ask: Moses our teacher should have hastened to circumcise first, for circumcision carries the penalty of excision (כרת), whereas the journey to Egypt involved only an act — one may answer: the excision is not incumbent upon the father but upon the uncircumcised person himself, as it is written 'and an uncircumcised male who does not circumcise the flesh of his foreskin, that soul shall be cut off, etc.' (וערל זכר אשר לא ימול בשר ערלתו ונכרתה וגו׳). Therefore he was lax in it and occupied himself with the lodging first, and because he was lax in it — 'and He sought to put him to death.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "Citation is Hosea 13:8, not 3:18 as written in the Hebrew text.", 2 "המקום (lit. 'the Place') is a rabbinic designation for God."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:16.296931822Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}